        <mxCell id="header-sub" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#1e293b&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;What happens, in order, between a pod on a public cloud and the panel a project dev reads in Grafana?&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;Scope: one metric and one log line of an app on the public cloud target (EKS or GKE, same steps), then the dev&amp;#39;s dashboard query · cloud side as in Cloud#50 (wave V6, open), hub side as on K3s main of 2026-11-21 · derived from code (Cloud/terraform/public/platform/observability, K3s/k8s/config/{wireguard,observability}/vmauth-clouds.yaml)&lt;br&gt;Out of scope: on-prem collection and audit (see observability) · traces (observability-multicloud) · alerting · OpenCost&lt;br&gt;Arrows: plain = request, dashed = reply. Notes in grey say what checks or rewrites the data.&lt;br&gt;v0.3 (2026-11-21: vmagent, Fluent Bit, vmauth-clouds and VMSingle replace Alloy, Loki and the VictoriaMetrics cluster, CNP-276) · source: cnp-docs/architecture/cnp&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
